WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.048
Sections seven and eight use the same assessment framework as the preceding sessions: establish the individual baseline, identify the new change and choose a specific modification.
第七、八节沿用前面框架：建立个体基线、识别新变化，再选择具体调整。

00:00:12.048 --> 00:00:23.184
The task is not to memorize a list of diseases associated with obesity. Explain which mechanism could affect this patient, what evidence you seek and how that changes care.
任务不是背一串与肥胖有关的病名，而是解释哪个机制可能影响这个人、需找什么证据，以及如何改变照护。

00:00:23.184 --> 00:00:34.968
Airway preparation, safe positioning and an extraction plan should start early. Waiting until a patient deteriorates can make a previously manageable access problem much harder.
气道准备、安全体位及脱困计划应及早开始。等患者恶化后，原本可处理的接近问题可能难得多。

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:47.736
The movement principles here do not certify use of a lifting device or replace its instructions. Actual equipment, local procedures, team training and the clinical situation determine the safe method.
这里的移动原则不构成吊运器械资质，也不替代其说明。安全方法取决于真实器械、当地程序、团队训练及临床情境。

00:00:47.736 --> 00:00:59.472
Use neutral, person-centered language and ask how the patient prefers to be addressed. Avoid jokes, blame or conversations about the patient as though they were not present.
应使用中性、以人为中心的语言，并询问偏好称呼。避免玩笑、责备，或当患者不存在般讨论他。

00:00:59.472 --> 00:01:10.416
Explain that additional equipment or personnel are being requested to support safe care. Do not describe the patient as the problem or promise that a difficult move will be effortless.
要解释增派器械或人员是为了安全照护，不能把患者说成问题本身，也不要承诺困难移动毫不费力。

00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:22.584
Size does not tell you whether someone can walk, understands a decision or has a particular illness. Ask, observe and assess instead of substituting a stereotype for evidence.
体型不能告诉你此人是否能走、理解决定或患有某病。需询问、观察及评估，不用刻板印象替代证据。

00:01:22.584 --> 00:01:34.200
Expose only what is needed, provide appropriate covering and seek permission for sensitive examination. Urgent care can still include a clear explanation and respectful handling.
只暴露必要部位，适当覆盖，并为敏感检查取得同意。紧急照护仍可有清楚解释及尊重的搬运。

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:45.192
Ask how the patient normally transfers and what assistance or devices are used. A usual independent transfer does not prove that it remains safe during the present illness.
要问平时如何转移、使用什么协助或器械。平时能独立转移，不证明这次生病时仍然安全。

00:01:45.192 --> 00:01:56.736
Clarify usual breathing, tolerated sleeping position and prescribed respiratory support. Ask what is different today, including new inability to lie back or a change in alertness.
需澄清平时呼吸、能耐受的睡姿及处方呼吸支持，并问今天不同之处，例如新出现不能后躺或清醒变化。

00:01:56.736 --> 00:02:10.848
Obtain the symptom timeline and associated findings without assuming all dyspnea is caused by size. Cardiac, infectious, thromboembolic, metabolic and drug-related illness can coexist.
应取得症状时间线及伴随发现，不能认定所有气促都是体型导致。心脏、感染、血栓栓塞、代谢及药物疾病可并存。

00:02:10.848 --> 00:02:22.512
A patient may know which approach previously worked or caused pain. Use that information in the plan while independently checking current physiology, equipment and environmental safety.
患者可能知道以往什么方法有效或会疼。计划应利用这些信息，同时独立检查当前生理、器械及环境安全。

00:02:22.512 --> 00:02:35.184
Additional chest-wall and abdominal loading can make expansion harder and reduce resting lung volume. The effect varies between patients and is not an identical physiological state in everyone.
胸壁及腹部负荷增加可使扩张更困难，并降低静息肺容量。但影响因人而异，不是人人都处于相同生理状态。

00:02:35.184 --> 00:02:46.968
When the patient lies flat, abdominal contents may further limit diaphragm movement. New orthopnea or worsening effort during repositioning is a clinical finding to act on.
平躺时，腹腔内容物可能进一步限制膈肌活动。调整体位时新出现端坐呼吸或用力增加，是需要采取行动的临床发现。

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:59.952
Reduced reserve means oxygen levels may fall quickly when breathing stops or an airway intervention interrupts ventilation. Anticipation is useful, but it does not predict an exact safe apnea time.
储备较少意味着停止呼吸或气道操作中断通气后，氧水平可能迅速下降。应提前准备，但不能据此预测准确安全呼吸暂停时间。

00:02:59.952 --> 00:03:12.384
Assess actual ventilation rather than count a respiratory rate alone. Chest movement, depth, air entry, responsiveness and the trend help identify inadequate breathing.
需评估真实通气，不只数呼吸频率。胸部活动、深度、气流、反应及趋势有助识别呼吸不足。

00:03:12.384 --> 00:03:25.224
A saturation reading estimates oxygenation and does not directly measure carbon dioxide or airway protection. Supplemental oxygen can improve that number while ventilation remains inadequate.
血氧饱和度估计氧合，不能直接测二氧化碳或气道保护。给氧可能改善数值，但通气仍然不足。

00:03:25.224 --> 00:03:37.128
A patient who becomes increasingly drowsy with shallow breathing needs urgent assessment even if a displayed saturation appears acceptable. Do not let the monitor replace direct observation.
患者越来越嗜睡且呼吸浅，即使显示血氧看似可接受，也需紧急评估。不能让监护器替代直接观察。

00:03:37.128 --> 00:03:50.880
Use capnography when available, appropriate and authorized, recognizing its sampling and perfusion limitations. A single end-tidal number is not identical to an arterial blood-gas diagnosis.
有条件、适用且获授权时可用呼气末二氧化碳，同时认识采样及灌注限制。单次呼气末数值不等同动脉血气诊断。

00:03:50.880 --> 00:04:03.672
After changing position or assisting breathing, reassess movement, effort, responsiveness and reliable measurements. An intervention is only useful if its actual effect is checked.
改变体位或辅助呼吸后，需复查活动、用力、反应及可靠测量。只有核查真实效果，才能知道干预是否有效。

00:04:03.672 --> 00:04:14.640
Obstructive sleep apnea involves repeated upper-airway obstruction during sleep. Ask whether it is diagnosed and whether the patient uses prescribed positive-airway-pressure support.
阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停涉及睡眠中反复上气道阻塞。需问是否已诊断，以及是否使用处方正压支持。

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:27.120
Snoring, witnessed pauses and daytime sleepiness can be useful history, but they do not establish the diagnosis by themselves. Not every larger-bodied patient has sleep apnea.
打鼾、目击呼吸暂停及日间困倦是有用病史，但单凭这些不能确诊，也不是每个大体型患者都有睡眠呼吸暂停。

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:36.912
New confusion, severe breathlessness or failure to remain awake should not be labelled normal sleep apnea without assessing immediate threats and other causes.
新混乱、严重气促或无法保持清醒，不能未经评估即时威胁及其他原因就称正常睡眠呼吸暂停。

00:04:36.912 --> 00:04:50.904
A home device does not automatically provide appropriate emergency ventilation. Check the current condition, actual equipment and applicable pathway rather than simply place an unresponsive patient on their usual mask.
家用器械不自动提供适当急救通气。需检查当前病情、真实器械及适用路径，不能只把平常面罩套在无反应患者身上。

00:04:50.904 --> 00:05:04.440
The ATS definition includes a body-mass index of at least thirty, sleep-disordered breathing and awake resting arterial carbon dioxide of at least forty-five millimeters of mercury after other causes are excluded.
ATS定义包括BMI至少三十、睡眠呼吸障碍，以及排除其他原因后，清醒静息动脉二氧化碳至少四十五毫米汞柱。

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:18.552
That is a diagnostic framework, not a prehospital label applied from appearance or a pulse-oximeter reading. Obesity, obstructive sleep apnea and obesity hypoventilation syndrome are related but distinct.
这是诊断框架，不是凭外观或指夹血氧即可贴上的院前标签。肥胖、阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停及肥胖低通气综合征相关，但并不相同。

00:05:18.552 --> 00:05:31.776
A normal-looking saturation does not establish normal carbon dioxide, and suspected chronic disease does not explain away acute deterioration. Other causes of hypoventilation still matter.
看似正常的血氧不证明二氧化碳正常，疑似慢病也不能解释掉急性恶化。其他低通气原因仍然重要。

00:05:31.776 --> 00:05:44.760
For this lesson, the action is to recognize and support failing breathing through the authorized pathway. Long-term testing, PAP prescriptions and weight-management treatment are not being prescribed here.
本节的行动是识别呼吸衰竭，并依授权路径提供支持。这里不制定长期检查、正压处方或体重管理治疗。

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:58.344
The school connects severe obesity with hypertension, increased cardiac workload, ischemic disease and heart failure. These are possible associated risks, not diagnoses guaranteed in every patient.
学校将重度肥胖与高血压、心脏负荷增加、缺血及心衰相连。这些是可能的相关风险，不是每个患者必然具有的诊断。

00:05:58.344 --> 00:06:14.328
Ask about new chest discomfort, breathlessness, exertional limitation, swelling and the time course. Diabetes or other disease may alter symptoms, but absence of classic pain does not exclude an acute coronary problem.
应问新胸部不适、气促、活动受限、水肿及时间线。糖尿病等可改变症状，但缺乏典型疼痛不排除急性冠脉问题。

00:06:14.328 --> 00:06:26.952
Difficulty seeing neck veins or hearing crackles does not prove their absence or exclude failure. State the examination limitation and combine other findings and appropriate monitoring.
难以看清颈静脉或听到啰音，不证明它们不存在，也不排除心衰。应说明检查限制，结合其他发现与合适监测。

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:38.328
Do not give fluid simply because the examination is difficult or assume all edema is new cardiac failure. The physiological problem and authorized care pathway determine treatment.
不能因检查困难就给液，也不能认所有水肿都是新心衰。治疗需由真实生理问题及授权路径决定。

00:06:38.328 --> 00:06:49.416
Shock can develop in a patient of any size. An unobtainable or unreliable blood pressure is missing information, not proof of adequate perfusion.
任何体型都可发生休克。测不到或不可靠的血压代表资料缺失，不是灌注充分的证据。

00:06:49.416 --> 00:07:01.224
Use responsiveness, peripheral findings, pulse, breathing and appropriate repeated measurements together. A normal-range pressure does not by itself rule out a developing emergency.
需综合反应、外周发现、脉搏、呼吸及适当重复测量。单个范围内血压不能排除正在发展的急症。

00:07:01.224 --> 00:07:12.984
Search for the plausible mechanism, including bleeding, infection, cardiac dysfunction and obstructive causes. Size can complicate detection without being the cause of the illness.
需寻找合理机制，包括出血、感染、心功能异常及阻塞性原因。体型可使发现更困难，却未必是疾病原因。

00:07:12.984 --> 00:07:25.680
Explain uncertainty during consultation or handover and repeat the assessment after care or movement. Do not invent a reassuring normal finding when the examination could not establish it.
会诊或交接时需解释不确定性，照护或移动后重复评估。无法证实时，不能编造一个令人放心的正常发现。

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:36.288
Soft tissue, neck mobility and respiratory mechanics can make airway management more difficult, but difficulty must be assessed rather than assumed solely from weight.
软组织、颈部活动及呼吸力学可增加气道管理困难，但需实际评估，不能只凭体重假定。

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:47.520
Bring suction and appropriate authorized airway equipment into reach. Assign help early when positioning, mask seal or ventilation will require more than one provider.
应把吸引及合适授权气道器械放到可及处。体位、面罩密封或通气需多人时，应及早安排帮助。

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:58.752
Choose the least invasive effective approach and verify its effect. Oxygen delivery alone does not reopen every obstruction or provide breaths to an apneic patient.
应选择最少侵入但有效的方法，并核实效果。单纯给氧不能解除所有阻塞，也不能为呼吸暂停患者提供呼吸。

00:07:58.752 --> 00:08:11.664
Advanced airway procedures remain role- and situation-dependent. Preparing for difficulty does not make an uncredentialed intervention appropriate or justify delay in basic ventilation.
高级气道操作仍取决于角色及情境。预计困难，不等于未获资质操作合理，也不能成为延误基本通气的理由。

00:08:11.664 --> 00:08:24.768
The school ramped position elevates the head and upper torso with stable support. The external ear canal and sternal notch are brought toward the same horizontal level rather than forcing the neck into flexion.
学校的斜坡体位是以稳定支撑抬高头及上躯干，使外耳道与胸骨切迹接近同一水平，而不是强迫颈部屈曲。

00:08:24.768 --> 00:08:36.672
Use equipment and supports that remain stable under the actual load. Check that the adjustment improves airway access and breathing instead of leaving the chin compressed toward the chest.
应使用在实际负荷下仍稳定的器械及支撑，并检查调整是否改善气道与呼吸，而非让下巴压向胸前。

00:08:36.672 --> 00:08:48.480
An awake breathless patient may prefer a supported upright position. The best position depends on airway protection, perfusion, injury constraints and what can safely be maintained.
清醒气促者可能更适合有支撑的坐位。最佳体位取决于气道保护、灌注、伤情限制及能否安全维持。

00:08:48.480 --> 00:09:01.128
Ramping for an airway is not a universal position for cardiac arrest or every trauma. Use the applicable resuscitation and injury requirements, and reassess the effect of any change.
气道斜坡体位不是所有心脏骤停或创伤的通用体位。需遵循相应复苏及伤情要求，并复查每次调整的效果。

00:09:01.128 --> 00:09:13.248
When breathing is inadequate, follow the appropriate airway and assisted-ventilation pathway. Address patency and use a suitable interface rather than simply increase oxygen flow.
呼吸不足时，应依相应气道及辅助通气路径处理通畅，并使用合适接口，而不是只增加氧流量。

00:09:13.248 --> 00:09:24.504
Two-provider mask ventilation can separate airway positioning and seal from bag operation. Allocate tasks and observe whether each breath produces useful chest movement.
双人面罩通气可把气道体位及密封与挤囊分开。需分配任务，并观察每次呼吸是否产生有效胸部活动。

00:09:24.504 --> 00:09:38.856
Excess force or speed can cause harm and does not solve every poor seal or obstruction. If effect is poor, reassess the airway, device, position and possible causes rather than repeatedly squeeze harder.
过度用力或过快可能有害，也不能解决每种漏气或阻塞。效果差时应复评气道、器械、体位及原因，而非反复更用力挤。

00:09:38.856 --> 00:09:52.080
Continue the appropriate ventilation rate, monitoring and escalation for the clinical situation. This session adds positioning considerations, not an obesity-specific replacement resuscitation algorithm.
应按临床情境继续适当频率、监测及升级。本节增加体位考虑，不另造一套肥胖专用复苏算法。

00:09:52.080 --> 00:10:05.280
The school stresses early oxygen preparation because reserve may be limited. That should not be translated into permanent high-flow oxygen for every patient regardless of oxygenation or clinical state.
学校因储备可能较少而强调早准备氧气，但不能把它翻译成无论氧合或状态如何，人人都持续高流量氧。

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:18.384
Use the applicable oxygen pathway, device and reliable measurements while treating immediate threats. Severe hypoxemia or resuscitation may require urgent rescue oxygen and ventilation.
需按适用氧路径、器械及可靠测量处理即时威胁。严重低氧或复苏可能需要紧急救援给氧及通气。

00:10:18.384 --> 00:10:32.112
Do not apply a COPD-specific target merely because someone has obesity, OSA or possible carbon-dioxide retention. Establish the relevant clinical history and use the actual authorized pathway.
不能因肥胖、OSA或可能二氧化碳潴留，就自动套COPD目标。应澄相关病史，并用真实授权路径。

00:10:32.112 --> 00:10:45.192
Never withhold necessary support through fear of a simplified hypoxic-drive story. Reassess consciousness and ventilation as well as saturation and arrange the resources the patient needs.
不能因简化的低氧驱动故事而扣住所需支持。需同时复评意识、通气及血氧，并安排所需资源。

00:10:45.192 --> 00:10:57.384
Choose a cuff whose stated range fits the measured arm. A cuff that is too small can overestimate pressure; a poor fit or incorrect technique can make a numerical result unreliable.
应依实测臂围选择标示范围合适的袖带。过小袖带可高估血压；不贴合或技术错误可使数字不可靠。

00:10:57.384 --> 00:11:09.672
Support the limb and use the appropriate measurement position and device instructions. The biggest available cuff is not automatically correct if it is applied poorly or outside its supported range.
需支撑肢体，并依合适位置及器械说明测量。现有最大袖带若使用错误或超出支持范围，也不自动正确。

00:11:09.672 --> 00:11:21.144
If a standard upper-arm measurement is not possible, follow the approved alternative and record where and how it was obtained. Do not quietly treat a different site as an identical measurement.
若标准上臂无法测量，需按批准替代方法，并记录部位及方式。不能不加说明地把不同部位当完全相同测量。

00:11:21.144 --> 00:11:33.744
Combine perfusion findings and repeated observations while seeking a reliable value. Failed measurement is not a normal pressure, and a corrected reading does not erase the clinical examination.
寻求可靠值时，应结合灌注及重复观察。测量失败不是血压正常，纠正后的读数也不能抹去临床检查。

00:11:33.744 --> 00:11:44.640
Heart and lung sounds may be harder to hear through tissue or background noise. Improve positioning, reduce noise and repeat relevant areas with suitable equipment.
组织及背景噪声可使心肺音难听。需改善位置、降低噪声，并用合适器械重复相关部位。

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:55.680
Do not use painful pressure or abandon the examination without explanation. Ask about discomfort and obtain help when access or positioning limits a useful assessment.
不能使用疼痛性压力，也不能毫无解释地放弃检查。需问不适，接近或体位限制有效检查时寻求帮助。

00:11:55.680 --> 00:12:10.320
Combine the examination with observed effort, chest movement, reliable oxygenation, pulse, pressure and symptoms. No single normal-looking finding excludes an important respiratory or cardiac emergency.
需结合用力、胸动、可靠氧合、脉搏、血压及症状。任何单个看似正常发现，都不能排除重要呼吸或心脏急症。

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:21.360
Document a sound as difficult to assess when that is true. Describing an uncertain result as clear lungs can mislead the next clinician and alter the treatment plan.
确实难评时，就记录难以评估。把不确定结果写成双肺清晰，会误导下位临床人员并影响计划。

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:34.488
The school describes lower ECG amplitude in some larger-bodied patients, but its phrase normal artifact is too reassuring. A genuinely small signal is not the same thing as electrical noise.
学校提到部分大体型者心电幅度较低，但称正常伪差过度令人放心。真实小信号，与电噪声不是同一回事。

00:12:34.488 --> 00:12:47.976
Check the actual acquisition process, including lead placement, contact, motion and device settings. Correct a technical problem and reassess without inventing a new calibration convention.
需检查真实采集过程，包括导联位置、接触、活动及器械设置。纠正技术问题并复查，不能自行另造校准规则。

00:12:47.976 --> 00:13:01.536
Interpret the ECG with symptoms and perfusion, and seek the appropriate review when findings are uncertain. Body habitus does not independently explain every low-amplitude or abnormal tracing.
需结合症状及灌注解释心电，不确定时寻求适当复核。体型不能独立解释每张低幅或异常图形。

00:13:01.536 --> 00:13:14.832
A nondiagnostic ECG does not rule out acute coronary disease. Continue the indicated clinical pathway and conveyance plan rather than dismiss new chest or breathing symptoms as weight-related.
非诊断性心电不能排除急性冠脉病。需继续相应路径及转运计划，不把新胸部或呼吸症状说成体重问题。

00:13:14.832 --> 00:13:29.904
Skin folds and areas beneath devices may hide injury or infection. In a patient with relevant pain, fever, drainage or unexplained illness, ask about these areas and perform a proportionate examination.
皮褶及器械下方可藏伤或感染。相关疼痛、发热、渗液或原因不明疾病时，需询问并进行适度检查。

00:13:29.904 --> 00:13:42.216
Explain the reason, obtain appropriate permission, provide covering and ask how the patient can help safely. Avoid dragging or lifting tissue in a painful or damaging manner.
应解释原因、取得适当同意、提供覆盖，并问患者如何安全协助。避免以疼痛或损伤方式拖拉、提起组织。

00:13:42.216 --> 00:13:57.528
Record objective findings such as location, redness, open areas, drainage and tenderness. Odor alone does not identify an organism, and a visible wound is not proof that it explains all systemic symptoms.
需记录位置、红、破损、渗液及压痛等客观发现。气味不能单独识别病原，可见伤口也不证明解释全部全身症状。

00:13:57.528 --> 00:14:09.168
Protect skin during transfer and communicate concerns. Do not perform unapproved invasive wound treatment or delay urgent care to produce a complete photographic inventory.
转移中需保护皮肤并交接担忧。不能做未经授权侵入伤口处理，也不能为完整拍照清单延误急救。

00:14:09.168 --> 00:14:20.568
Deeper veins and difficulty identifying landmarks may make access harder. Begin by deciding whether access is indicated and whether it changes the immediate treatment plan.
较深静脉及标志难辨可增加通路困难。首先应判断是否有适应证，以及是否改变即时治疗计划。

00:14:20.568 --> 00:14:34.560
The school mentions longer catheters, ultrasound and alternatives. These are not interchangeable solutions or new permissions; the actual device, procedure, operator training and role must support their use.
学校提到长导管、超声及替代方法，但它们不能随意互换，也不产生新权限。使用需有真实器械、程序、训练及角色支持。

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:46.512
Follow attempt limits and escalation requirements. Do not repeatedly puncture, guess an inaccessible landmark or use a needle length selected only because the patient is large.
需遵守尝试次数及升级要求。不能反复穿刺、猜不可辨标志，或只因体型大就选择针长。

00:14:46.512 --> 00:14:59.424
Continue the primary care and conveyance plan while resources are arranged. Vascular access is a means to indicated care, not a task that must be completed before leaving every scene.
安排资源时仍需继续主要照护及转运计划。通路是提供适应照护的手段，不是每次离场前必须完成的任务。

00:14:59.424 --> 00:15:10.296
Some medicines use weight, some use a fixed dose and some have a ceiling. A larger patient does not automatically receive a proportional increase in every drug.
部分药按体重、部分固定剂量、部分有上限。患者更大，不等于所有药都按比例增加。

00:15:10.296 --> 00:15:23.184
If a protocol specifies actual, ideal or adjusted weight, use that defined method and an appropriate verified weight source. Do not invent a substitution from a general obesity lecture.
若协议指定实际、理想或调整体重，需用其定义方法及适当核实体重来源，不能从一般肥胖课自行替换。

00:15:23.184 --> 00:15:37.680
Confirm indication, product, concentration, route, maximum and authorization before calculation. Estimating body size by eye is not a reliable substitute for the required weight method.
计算前应确认适应证、产品、浓度、途径、上限及授权。目测体型不是所需体重方法的可靠替代。

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:48.408
Check the clinical response and adverse effects after permitted treatment. The practical goal is correct patient-specific care, not a general rule to give more medication.
获准治疗后需查临床反应及不良作用。实际目标是正确个体照护，不是一条多给药的通则。

00:15:48.408 --> 00:16:00.648
A movement assessment combines the patient's current clinical needs with the physical task. A conscious patient may still be unsafe to walk because of instability, injury or severe breathlessness.
移动评估需结合当前临床需要及身体任务。清醒患者仍可能因不稳定、伤或严重气促而不宜走。

00:16:00.648 --> 00:16:11.256
Define the actual transfer: from floor, chair or bed; across which surfaces; through which route; and with what ongoing airway or monitoring needs.
应定义真实转移：从地面、椅或床开始，跨什么表面、经什么路线，以及需持续哪些气道或监测支持。

00:16:11.256 --> 00:16:24.000
Assess space, stairs, obstacles, weather and the destination loading process. A device that fits beside a bed may not fit through the planned doorway or onto the next platform.
需评空间、楼梯、障碍、天气及终点装载。能放床边的器械，未必能通过计划门口或接上下个平台。

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:36.864
Use appropriate controls and trained equipment rather than assume more manual lifters make any task safe. If the plan cannot be performed safely, change the plan and request the right resources.
需使用适当控制及训练器械，不能以为多加人工就能使任何任务安全。计划无法安全执行时，要改计划并请求正确资源。

00:16:36.864 --> 00:16:50.040
Invite the patient to describe a usual transfer and any painful or ineffective previous methods. Participation should preserve autonomy, not shift responsibility for an unsafe task onto them.
应请患者描述平时转移，以及以往疼痛或无效的方法。让其参与是保自主，不是把不安全任务责任推给他。

00:16:50.040 --> 00:17:01.416
A verbal assurance of being able to walk is not the whole assessment. Check clinical suitability, observed function and the route, using the approved staged method when appropriate.
口头保证能走，不是完整评估。需查临床适宜、实际功能及路线，适用时用获准分阶段方法。

00:17:01.416 --> 00:17:12.480
Do not force a walk test in a patient with serious cardiac, respiratory or injury concerns. Use appropriate nonambulatory support and additional help when indicated.
有严重心脏、呼吸或伤情担忧时，不能强迫试走。适应时应使用合适非步行支持及增援。

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:25.200
If unexpected assistance or unsafe effort is needed, stop and reassess. The patient's wish to avoid embarrassment is important, but it does not make an unstable transfer safe.
需要超预期协助或出现不安全用力时，应停止复评。患者希望避免尴尬很重要，但这不会使不稳定转移变安全。

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:36.000
Inspect the whole route, not only the first doorway. Consider turning space, stair geometry and the room needed for operators to use the chosen equipment correctly.
应检查整条路线，不只第一个门口。需考虑转弯空间、楼梯形态及操作人员正确使用器械所需空间。

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:45.816
Check the surfaces and loading points the equipment will cross. Weight limits and support requirements apply to every component, not just the main stretcher.
需检查器械经过的表面及装载点。重量限制及支撑要求适用于每个部件，不只主担架。

00:17:45.816 --> 00:17:58.944
Plan how oxygen, monitoring, airway access and attachments remain protected. A transfer that loses necessary ventilation or pulls out a line is not successful merely because the patient moved.
应计划如何保护氧气、监测、气道接近及附件。移动中失去必要通气或拔掉通路，不能只因人搬了就算成功。

00:17:58.944 --> 00:18:11.232
When the route or structure makes the task unsafe, seek appropriate specialist resources and a safer alternative. Do not improvise structural changes or unsupported lifting methods.
路线或结构使任务不安全时，应寻求适当专业资源及更安全替代。不能临时采用无支持的改结构或吊运方法。

00:18:11.232 --> 00:18:21.720
Use the actual manufacturer rating and local procedure for every device. A remembered number from another stretcher or a verbal guess is not a capacity check.
每件器械都需依真实制造商额定及当地程序。记得另一副担架的数值或口头猜测，不是容量核查。

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:31.752
Fit matters as well as mass. Check width, limb support, securement, pressure points and whether the patient can maintain the necessary breathing position.
除质量外，贴合也重要。需查宽度、肢体支持、固定、受压点，以及是否能保持必要呼吸体位。

00:18:31.752 --> 00:18:45.408
A transfer sheet, lifting aid, stretcher and loading system have different functions. Confirm compatibility and limits for the whole sequence; one high-capacity item does not upgrade the others.
转移布、吊运辅助、担架及装载系统功能不同。需核全程兼容及限制；一件大容量物品不会提升其余器械额定。

00:18:45.408 --> 00:18:58.920
Inspect condition, power and required accessories and use trained operators. If the necessary equipment is absent, communicate the gap and arrange a safe alternative instead of gambling on a trial lift.
需检查状态、电源及必要附件，并由训练人员操作。缺器械时应说明缺口并安排安全替代，不能赌一次试抬。

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:08.832
Identify a team leader and explain the sequence before movement. Every team member should know who can stop the task and what signal means stop immediately.
移动前需指定队长并说明顺序。每位成员都应知道谁能叫停，以及哪个信号表示立即停止。

00:19:08.832 --> 00:19:21.648
Assign the patient communicator, airway or monitor responsibility, equipment operators and attachment checks. Avoid asking one person to perform incompatible jobs simultaneously.
需分配患者沟通、气道或监测、器械操作及附件检查。不要让一人同时承担无法兼顾的任务。

00:19:21.648 --> 00:19:33.216
Invite concerns before the load moves and confirm readiness. A team member who cannot see a hazard or reach a control needs the plan adjusted, not pressure to continue.
负荷移动前应邀请担忧并确认准备。有成员看不到危险或够不到控制时，应改计划，而不是施压继续。

00:19:33.216 --> 00:19:43.752
Use clear commands and controlled movement with the selected device. More people acting independently can increase risk; coordination and the correct equipment matter.
需清楚口令，并用所选器械受控移动。更多人各自行动可能增险，协调及正确器械才重要。

00:19:43.752 --> 00:19:55.440
Explain the next action to the patient and verify that the intended breathing support and monitoring can continue. Check equipment setup, route and team readiness before loading.
需向患者解释下一步，并核实呼吸支持及监测能继续。加载前应查器械、路线及团队准备。

00:19:55.440 --> 00:20:07.416
Move in a controlled coordinated manner using the device instructions. Friction-reducing aids can reduce shear and effort, but they are not all lifting devices and must not be used as if they were.
需依器械说明受控协调移动。减摩辅助可减剪切及用力，但并非全是吊具，不能当吊具使用。

00:20:07.416 --> 00:20:18.216
Observe the patient, not only the equipment. Protect limbs, skin and attachments and maintain covering without obstructing necessary airway access or monitoring.
应观察患者，不只看器械。需护肢体、皮肤及附件，并覆盖隐私，但不能阻碍必要气道接近或监测。

00:20:18.216 --> 00:20:29.736
At the receiving surface, verify securement, pressure areas, position and device connections. Recheck the important clinical findings before calling the transfer complete.
到接收表面后，需核固定、受压部位、体位及连接，并复查关键临床发现，再称转移完成。

00:20:29.736 --> 00:20:41.376
Stop the movement safely if the patient develops new respiratory distress, severe pain or reduced responsiveness. Resume the primary assessment and provide immediate support.
患者新出现呼吸窘迫、剧痛或反应下降时，需安全停止移动，重新主要评估并立即支持。

00:20:41.376 --> 00:20:52.008
Equipment instability, an uncertain load limit or a malfunction requires a changed plan. Do not test an uncertain limit with the patient as the load.
器械不稳、负荷上限不确定或故障，都需改计划。不能把患者当负荷去试未知上限。

00:20:52.008 --> 00:21:02.904
An unexpected obstacle or unsafe operator position is sufficient reason to pause. A partially completed transfer does not make the remaining unsafe step acceptable.
突然障碍或人员位置不安全，就足以暂停。已经转了一半，不代表余下危险步骤可接受。

00:21:02.904 --> 00:21:14.856
After stabilizing the situation, communicate what changed and request the appropriate help. Document the actual reason and alternative, without blaming the patient for the safety problem.
稳定后需说明变化并请求适当帮助。应记录真实原因及替代，不把安全问题归罪患者。

00:21:14.856 --> 00:21:26.688
Repeat breathing findings and confirm that the patient tolerates the new position. A previously useful ramp can shift during transfer and an oxygen connection can become ineffective.
需复查呼吸并确认耐受新体位。原本有效的斜坡可能转移后移位，氧气连接也可能失效。

00:21:26.688 --> 00:21:39.096
Check symptoms, responsiveness and relevant measurements against the pre-move findings. An improved pulse-oximeter number alone is not proof that the transfer caused no physiological harm.
应把症状、反应及相关测量与移动前比较。单个血氧改善，不证明转移没有产生生理影响。

00:21:39.096 --> 00:21:51.744
Look for painful pressure, trapped limbs, skin shear or disrupted attachments and correct safe reversible problems. Ask the patient directly about comfort and remaining concerns.
需找疼痛压力、肢体夹压、皮肤剪切及附件断开，并安全纠正可逆问题；直接问舒适及剩余担忧。

00:21:51.744 --> 00:22:03.264
Continue time-sensitive conveyance and explain adaptations at handover. Equipment and movement details should support continuity, not replace the clinical illness story.
应继续时间敏感转运，并在交接解释调整。器械移动细节应支持连续照护，而不是取代疾病故事。

00:22:03.264 --> 00:22:14.976
This is an original teaching example, not a school assessed scenario. A fifty-eight-year-old reports worsening breathlessness over two days and cannot tolerate lying back today.
这是原创教学例，不是学校考核病例。一名五十八岁者诉两天气促加重，今天不能耐受后躺。

00:22:14.976 --> 00:22:27.912
They report nocturnal CPAP and usually walk short distances independently. Those facts describe useful history; they do not establish the cause of this new illness or current walking safety.
本人报告夜间用CPAP，平时可独立短距离走。这些是有用病史，不证明新病原因或当前行走安全。

00:22:27.912 --> 00:22:39.888
The route includes a narrow stair turn, and the available stretcher capacity has not been verified. Unknown capacity remains unknown; do not assume the equipment is suitable.
路线有狭窄楼梯转弯，现有担架容量尚未核实。未知仍未知，不能假定器械合适。

00:22:39.888 --> 00:22:49.416
State two simultaneous priorities: assess and support the clinical problem, and arrange a safe movement solution before attempting extraction.
需说出两个同步优先：评估支持临床问题，并在尝试脱困前安排安全移动方案。

00:22:49.416 --> 00:23:02.448
Assume the patient is alert but speaks in short phrases with increased effort, a respiratory rate of thirty and pulse of one hundred twelve. A reliable room-air saturation is eighty-nine percent.
假设患者清醒，但用短句说话且用力增加，呼吸三十、脉搏一百一十二，可靠室内空气血氧八十九。

00:23:02.448 --> 00:23:16.368
A pressure of one hundred seventy-six over one hundred two was obtained with a visibly undersized cuff. Treat that reading as questionable and seek a suitable measurement rather than declare a hypertensive diagnosis.
一百七十六比一百零二由明显过小袖带取得。应把它当存疑读数并寻合适测量，而不是直接宣布高血压诊断。

00:23:16.368 --> 00:23:27.864
Lung sounds are difficult to assess in the noisy room and weight is not verified. Neither missing finding should be turned into a normal examination or a confident dose calculation.
嘈杂房间中肺音难评，体重未核实。不能把缺失发现变正常检查或有把握的剂量计算。

00:23:27.864 --> 00:23:39.720
Prioritize breathing support and a focused cardiac, respiratory and other-cause assessment. The history of CPAP does not prove that sleep apnea explains this acute dyspnea.
需优先呼吸支持，并重点评心脏、呼吸及其他原因。CPAP病史不证明睡眠呼吸暂停解释这次急气促。

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:51.480
Maintain a supported position that helps breathing while providing indicated authorized oxygen and airway care. Reassess the effect, and arrange escalation for failing breathing.
应维持有助呼吸的支撑体位，提供有适应证的授权给氧及气道照护，并复评效果；呼吸衰竭时安排升级。

00:23:51.480 --> 00:24:04.224
Continue relevant examination, measurements and ECG without delaying essential care. Seek a useful symptom and medicine history while acknowledging the uncertainty in the initial pressure.
需继续相关检查、测量及心电，不延误必要照护。应取有用症药史，同时承认初始血压不确定。

00:24:04.224 --> 00:24:16.080
Do not ask this acutely breathless patient to negotiate the stairs merely because they usually walk. Do not perform a trial lift with equipment whose capacity and route fit remain unknown.
不能因平时会走就要求这位急气促者上下楼，也不能用容量及路线贴合未知的器械试抬。

00:24:16.080 --> 00:24:28.392
Request the appropriate rated system, trained personnel and route solution. Continue clinical care while preparation occurs and communicate if urgency requires a revised coordinated plan.
应请求合适额定系统、训练人员及路线方案。准备时仍持续临床照护，紧迫程度改变时需沟通并协调改计划。

00:24:28.392 --> 00:24:39.504
Now assume oxygen has increased the displayed saturation to ninety-five percent, but the patient becomes drowsier with shallow and less effective chest movement.
现假设给氧后显示血氧升至九十五，但患者更嗜睡，胸部活动浅且较无效。

00:24:39.504 --> 00:24:50.616
That is not recovery merely because the oxygen number improved. Reassess airway protection and ventilation immediately and check the device and the actual clinical response.
不能只因氧数字改善就称恢复。需立即复评气道保护及通气，并检查器械与真实临床反应。

00:24:50.616 --> 00:25:02.664
Provide the authorized ventilatory support and escalation the findings require. Do not wait for a saturation collapse or diagnose OHS from the change without further evidence.
应依发现提供所需授权通气支持及升级。不能等血氧崩落，也不能无进一步证据就凭此诊断OHS。

00:25:02.664 --> 00:25:13.800
Reevaluate the movement plan with the additional airway needs. The team must protect effective care throughout extraction rather than prioritize finishing the original route unchanged.
需按新增气道需求重评移动计划。团队需在脱困全程保护有效照护，而不是优先原样完成原路线。

00:25:13.800 --> 00:25:26.328
Report what changed, when and from which baseline, including the patient's usual mobility and reported respiratory support. Avoid using bariatric patient as the entire clinical description.
应报告何时、相对什么基线发生何变化，包括平时活动及转述呼吸支持。不能用肥胖患者四字代替完整临床描述。

00:25:26.328 --> 00:25:37.680
Distinguish reliable measurements from the questionable cuff reading and limited auscultation. Describe the new drowsiness and shallow breathing even though saturation increased.
需区分可靠测量、存疑袖带值及受限听诊。即使血氧升高，也要描述新嗜睡与浅呼吸。

00:25:37.680 --> 00:25:48.432
Explain care and its actual effect, including ventilation and positioning. A list of equipment without a response does not show whether the immediate threat improved.
应解释照护及真实效果，包括通气与体位。只有器械清单而无反应，不能显示即时威胁是否改善。

00:25:48.432 --> 00:26:00.192
Communicate required movement support and unresolved gaps so the receiving team can prepare. Preserve privacy and clinical relevance when sharing size or equipment information.
需交接移动支持及未解缺口，使接收团队可准备。分享体型或器械资料时应保护隐私并保持临床相关。

00:26:00.192 --> 00:26:12.984
You should now connect the school mechanisms to observable findings without diagnosing from size. Distinguish OSA from OHS and technical ECG problems from an unexplained true small signal.
现在应能把学校机制连到可见发现，不凭体型诊断；需区分OSA与OHS，以及技术性心电问题与未解释真实小信号。

00:26:12.984 --> 00:26:24.408
Explain how cuff fit, access, skin folds and difficult sounds affect certainty. Missing information must stay visible rather than become a confident normal examination.
需解释袖带贴合、通路、皮褶及难听声音如何影响确定性。缺失资料必须可见，不能变成确信正常检查。

00:26:24.408 --> 00:26:38.016
In supervised practice, demonstrate appropriate ramping, the movement assessment and use of the actual equipment. State capacity, route, team roles and stop criteria before movement.
监督练习中应演示适当斜坡体位、移动评估及真实器械使用，移动前说清容量、路线、角色及停止条件。

00:26:38.016 --> 00:26:49.728
Finally, show how reassessment and a respectful handover protect the whole plan. The next session applies assessment modifications to pregnancy and obstetric red flags.
最后需说明复评及尊重的交接如何保护整体计划。下一节把评估调整用于妊娠及产科红旗。
